From: mix2-port <mix2@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath10k: skip quiet mode for WCN3990

Sending WMI_PDEV_SET_QUIET_MODE to WCN3990 crashes the firmware's WLAN
process (PDM: 'EX:wlan_process:1:WLAN RT:...'), which then takes the
modem down through its watchdog. The THERM_THROT service bit does not
reliably tell whether the firmware copes with it (seen on the Xiaomi
Mi MIX 2 with WLAN.HL.1.0 and on HL3.2), so never send it to WCN3990.

Based on the workaround proposed on linux-wireless in March 2026.
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/thermal.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/thermal.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/thermal.c
@@ -136,6 +136,10 @@ void ath10k_thermal_set_throttling(struct ath10k *ar)
 	if (!ar->wmi.ops->gen_pdev_set_quiet_mode)
 		return;
 
+	/* The WCN3990 firmware crashes on the quiet mode command */
+	if (QCA_REV_WCN3990(ar))
+		return;
+
 	if (ar->state != ATH10K_STATE_ON)
 		return;
 
